# Inference debug suite (`det3d/extra/infer_debug/`)

Trigger when the user asks for help debugging **inference alignment**: seg/bbox vs image, cascade post desync, `InvP`/`Fill`/`R`/`Off` suspects, or roundtrip validation.

## First read

[`det3d/extra/infer_debug/README.md`](det3d/extra/infer_debug/README.md)

## Default workflow

1. **Stepwise report** (no model weights):
   ```bash
   conda run -n dl python -m det3d.extra.infer_debug.run --fixture pseudo_cuboid
   conda run -n dl python -m det3d.extra.infer_debug.run --fixture lidc_0001
   ```
2. Inspect `{out}/{fixture}/{run_p}/patch_stages.tsv` and `cascade_stages.tsv` — first `pred_fg` or `n_boxes` change pinpoints the transform.
3. **Pseudo must PASS** (exact fg). **lidc_0001** may CHECK on full fg (spacing resample); per-lesion component masks are the primary assert.

## Fixtures

| Name | Use |
|------|-----|
| `pseudo_cuboid` | Stand-in image + 2 cuboid lesions; native spacing = plan spacing |
| `lidc_0001` | Real `/media/UB/datasets/lidc_all/`; 2 lesions (`ignore_labels=[6]`) |

## Interactive (real model)

[`det3d/inference/cascade.py`](det3d/inference/cascade.py) and [`patch.py`](det3d/inference/patch.py) `__main__` `# %%` blocks — stepwise with `ImageMaskBboxViewer`, GT CC in §6.

